window.docContents[35].resolve({"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___TorusNote___torus_subcoulomb_commutator":{"contents":"Let  be an integer and .There are , depending only on . Let  be real with . Let  be an integer and let  be pairwise distinct.For , let  be Lipschitz withFor ,The quantity in parentheses is nonnegative. The mixed and background integrals defining  and  converge absolutely.The torus is , with unit-volume Haar measure. The mean-zero periodic kernel has coefficientswhereThe kernel and its gradient are the heat-regularized limits. Their singular normalization is  for  and  for .Set . The energy and first transport commutator areThe integrals expand into the particle sum with  omitted, the mixed terms and the background term. All vector norms are Euclidean.In the transport bound,  is the Lipschitz seminorm for the quotient Euclidean distance. Each fractional-derivative norm is the norm of a representative  satisfyingwith Fourier convention , including .\n\nVerification: Lean proof term available; used in the verified all-regime estimate.\n\nSource: HRS/Commutator/Torus/Assembly.lean.\n\nDeclaration type, as written:\n\ntheorem torus_subcoulomb_commutator (hd : 3 ≤ d) {s : ℝ} (hs0 : 0 ≤ s) (hsd : s < (d : ℝ) - 2) :\n    ∃ C C₀ : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ 0 < C₀ ∧ ∀ ρ : Torus d → ℝ, Integrable ρ → MemLp ρ ⊤ volume →\n      ∫ x, ρ x = 1 → ∀ (v : Torus d → Euc d) (K : ℝ), TorusSubTransport d s v K →\n      ∀ (N : ℕ) (X : Config d N), 1 ≤ N → X ∉ collisionSet d N →\n        EnergyIntegrableT s X ρ ∧ CommIntegrableT s X ρ v ∧\n        0 ≤ modEnergyT s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamT d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n              C₀ * normT ⊤ ρ * lamT d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) ∧\n        |commAT s X ρ v| ≤ C * K *\n          (modEnergyT s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamT d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n            C₀ * normT ⊤ ρ * lamT d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s))\n\n\nInspected Lean proof body:\n\nby\n  obtain ⟨C, hC, S⟩ := subcoulomb_commutator_scale_T hd hs0 hsd\n  obtain ⟨Cp, hCp, S'⟩ := S ⊤ (by simp)\n  refine ⟨C, 2 * Cp, hC, by positivity, fun ρ h1 hinf hmass v K hv N X hN hX => ?_⟩\n  have hM1 := normT_top_ge_one ρ h1 hinf hmass\n  have hM : 0 < normT ⊤ ρ := lt_of_lt_of_le one_pos hM1\n  have hNpos : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast hN\n  have hd0 : (d : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by\n    have : (3 : ℝ) ≤ d := by exact_mod_cast hd\n    linarith\n  have hNM : 0 < (N : ℝ) * normT ⊤ ρ := mul_pos hNpos hM\n  have hlam : 0 < lamT d N ρ := Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hNM _\n  have hNM1 : 1 ≤ (N : ℝ) * normT ⊤ ρ := by\n    have hN1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ N := by exact_mod_cast hN\n    nlinarith\n  have hlam1 : lamT d N ρ ≤ 1 := by\n    unfold lamT\n    exact Real.rpow_le_one_of_one_le_of_nonpos hNM1 (by\n      have : (0 : ℝ) < d := by\n        have : (3 : ℝ) ≤ d := by exact_mod_cast hd\n        linarith\n      have : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 / d := by positivity\n      rw [neg_div]; linarith)\n  have hlamd : lamT d N ρ ^ (d : ℝ) = ((N : ℝ) * normT ⊤ ρ)⁻¹ := by\n    unfold lamT\n    rw [← Real.rpow_mul hNM.le, show (-(1 : ℝ) / d) * d = -1 by field_simp, Real.rpow_neg_one]\n  have hkey : lamT d N ρ ^ (-s) / (N : ℝ) = normT ⊤ ρ * lamT d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) := by\n    rw [sub_eq_add_neg, Real.rpow_add hlam, hlamd]\n    field_simp\n  obtain ⟨hE, hCI, hQ, hA⟩ := S' ρ h1 hinf hmass v K hv N X hN hX (lamT d N ρ) hlam hlam1\n  have hQe : scaleQT s Cp ⊤ (lamT d N ρ) X ρ =\n      modEnergyT s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamT d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n        2 * Cp * normT ⊤ ρ * lamT d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) := by\n    unfold scaleQT\n    simp only [ENNReal.inv_top, ENNReal.toReal_zero, sub_zero, mul_one]\n    rw [hkey]\n    ring\n  rw [hQe] at hQ hA\n  exact ⟨hE, hCI, hQ, hA⟩\n\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009The sharp sub-Coulomb commutator\u0009Lean declarations and evidence","header":"1.6.5. Torus · sharp-scale theorem","id":"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___TorusNote___torus_subcoulomb_commutator"}});